{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vep run [-h] [--engine {ensembl,vep-rs}] [--vep-cache VEP_CACHE]\n                          [--assembly {GRCh37,GRCh38,T2T-CHM13v2.0}] [--force]\n                          [--preset {everything,fast}] [--format {vcf,tab,json}] [-r REGION]\n                          [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --engine {ensembl,vep-rs}\n                        Engine: 'vep-rs' (default; fast Rust VEP, every platform) or 'ensembl'\n                        (Linux, macOS); each has its own cache\n  --vep-cache VEP_CACHE\n                        Path to VEP cache directory (e.g., $HOME/.vep)\n  --assembly {GRCh37,GRCh38,T2T-CHM13v2.0}\n                        Reference assembly for VEP (GRCh37, GRCh38 or T2T-CHM13v2.0)\n  --force               Force re-run even if output exists\n  --preset {everything,fast}\n                        What VEP annotates: 'everything' (default), or 'fast' (about twice as\n                        fast: consequences, genes, MANE transcripts, SIFT and PolyPhen; no\n                        population frequencies, for which use 'vcf gnomad', and no HGVS)\n  --format {vcf,tab,json}\n                        Output format (default: vcf)\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region (e.g. chrM, chrY:10000-20000)\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n6 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract vep run --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vep run --input sample.vcf.gz\n  wgsextract vep run --input sample.vcf.gz --assembly GRCh37 --format tab\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>_vep.vcf.gz (or .tsv/.json with --format), with VEP's summary.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, tabix, vep-rs; depending on options and inputs, also: samtools,\n  vep; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
